herwise i don't really  purchase any more hair accessories  number 21 is teeth whiteners oh my  goodness i cared so much about beauty  that i was willing to hurt myself for it  i had used teeth whiteners all the time  and my teeth would hurt i actually  damaged my enamel and now what i use is  coconut oil and baking soda you  basically mix it together and rub your  teeth with it like a toothpaste or oil  pulling oil pulling is basically where  you take coconut oil and you swish it  around your mouth and you do this every  single day for a while and then your  teeth actually get whiter i have done  this a few times and it works like magic  number 22 is one time clothing so if i  were to have some sort of an event where  i'm going to have to wear something that  i'm only going to wear for that one time  then i will now gear more towards  renting the item rather than purchasing  the item it can be much cheaper for you  even though you're spending money on an  item that you won't get to keep and  you're thinking oh that's such a waste  of money i might as well spend more  money and keep the item but you're gonna  keep the item take up more space and  you're not gonna use it so that's  definitely an option that i would  consider that may save you money in the  long run and space number 23 is  specialty cleaners you know like that  foaming toilet cleaner or that magic  degreaser i find that for me baking soda  vinegar and castol soap pretty much do  any cleaning job that i need number 24  is lunch when working this is actually  something that i used to do for years is  i would pack my lunch and take it to  work but now ever since i've heard of  intermittent fasting i have started too  fast when i'm working doing intermittent  fasting when i'm working means that i  don't have to prep a meal the day before  i don't have to pack it i don't have to  worry about having it cooled or heating  it up having to clean those containers  after i get back home and that time that  i would have spent eating i can either  spend it for myself or it's extra time  that i get to work so that i get to go  home earlier so for me it is a really  beneficial thing i don't ever buy lunch  when i'm working and lastly number 25 i  saved that controversial one for last it  is coffee shop coffees my husband and i  love a good cup of coffee but our  occasional visit to the coffee shop was  not the best use of our money i could  very well say that i removed coffee from  my life so that i could call myself a  minimalist but this is why i call it  controversial because i don't think that  minimalism is about just removing things  for the sake of removing them so that  you can say you own less i think it's  about removing excess removing those  things that either add burden or that  just don't necessarily add value to your  life so that you can make more room for  the things that do matter for those  things that do add joy and for me  drinking a latte is a very mindful  experience it brings me joy and comfort  and so it's not something that i want to  remove so instead of removing the coffee  we decided to buy an espresso machine so  that we never have to set foot in a  coffee shop again and truthfully i don't  even want to because  i think ours are better  so that is it for my 25 items that i no  longer buy i hope that this video has  been helpful for you if you enjoyed it  please give it a thumbs up and subscribe  so that you won't miss when i post a new  video i thank you so much for watching  and i can't wait to see you in the next  one bye for now

